{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, sorry you're locked out after the weekend. We can't offer you self-service reset because your account isn't set up for it yet, so we've asked a technician to set a temporary password for you. Once they approve it, they'll phone you at the number we have on file with the temporary password. We never send passwords by email or ticket. When you sign in with it, you'll be asked to pick a new password right away. It needs to be at least 14 characters and can't be one you've used recently. This works best at the Windows sign-in screen on your desktop while you're on the office network or VPN. Your account isn't locked, so you're all set once you get the call.",
  "internal_note": "Sender is grace.okafor@brightline.example (user_id 11), the account owner, writing from her own verified email. Not VIP. Account is active, failed_login_count 0, not locked, not blocked, must_change_password false. Not enrolled in Duo, so self-service reset isn't available. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days look clean: 10 sign-ins, all successful, all from New York (corporate 203.0.113.10 / residential 198.51.100.31), all during usual hours, no failures, no hosting networks. Following KB-002, I queued a password reset (approval id 1). It has not run yet. After approval, please phone the temp password to the number on file. No unlock needed. Small item: password_last_set is 2026-09-11 03:16 UTC (about 23:16 ET), outside her usual hours. Probably harmless, but worth confirming with her during the call. Also recommend enrolling her in Duo so she can use self-service reset next time.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-002",
    "KB-003"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
